 "doc": "a clamp yoke whose four bolt holes are ONE node with four parents",
 "meta": {
  "example": "02_shared_yoke",
  "header": [
   "A clamp yoke with four bolt holes -- and ONE bolt-hole node, named by four",
   "parents.",
   "",
   "THIS IS THE FILE THE NODE TABLE EXISTS FOR.  `Node.describe()` inlines",
   "children, so a nested-tree document would write the bolt feature four times",
   "and read it back as four independent copies; editing \"the\" hole would then",
   "move one of them.  Here `bolt` appears once and `h_mm`, `h_mp`, `h_pm`, `h_pp`",
   "each name it.  Deserialising constructs it exactly once and hands the SAME",
   "object to all four, so there is nothing to propagate: there is one node.",
   "",
   "WATCH IT HAPPEN",
   "  implexity model show models/02_shared_yoke.json",
   "      -- `bolt` is printed once, expanded, and marked `shared by 4`; the other",
   "         three parents print a back-reference instead of a second copy.",
   "  implexity model set models/02_shared_yoke.json bore_d=6.5 -o /tmp/yoke.json",
   "      -- ONE node parameter moves -- `bore.radius_mm` -- and all four holes",
   "         change, because the four translates name the same `bolt`, and that",
   "         one bolt contains that one bore.  There is nothing to propagate.",
   "",
   "SHARING IS BY IDENTITY, NEVER BY CONTENT.  The two `pad` nodes below are",
   "structurally identical and are NOT merged: the author wrote them separately,",
   "and content-deduplicating them would create a coupling nobody asked for --",
   "a later edit to one would silently move geometry the engineer was not looking",
   "at.  `implexity model show` reports 1 shared node here, not 2.",
   "",
   "TRY",
   "  implexity model show      models/02_shared_yoke.json",
   "  implexity model params    models/02_shared_yoke.json",
   "  implexity model set       models/02_shared_yoke.json bore_d=6.5 --dry-run",
   "  implexity model eval      models/02_shared_yoke.json --node bolt --grid 10"
  ],
  "teaches": "a shared subtree with four parents; sharing by identity, never by content"
 },
